.RE
.SS \fBnpm start\fP
.P
Runs the app in the development mode\.<br>
.br
Open http://localhost:3010 to view it in the browser\.
.br
Ensure PORT 3001 is accessible to support additional features\.
.P
The page will reload if you make edits\.<br>
.br
You will also see any lint errors in the console\.
.SS \fBnpm test\fP
.P
Launches the test runner in the interactive watch mode\.<br>
.br
See the section about 
.UR https://facebook.github.io/create-react-app/docs/running-tests
.I running tests
.UE
for more information\.
.SS \fBnpm run build\fP
.P
Builds the app for production to the \fBbuild\fP folder\.<br>
.br
It correctly bundles React in production mode and optimizes the build for the best performance\.
.P
The build is minified and the filenames include the hashes\.<br>
.br
Your app is ready to be deployed!
.P
See the section about 
.UR https://facebook.github.io/create-react-app/docs/deployment
.I deployment
.UE
for more information\.
.SS \fBnpm run build:lib\fP
.P
Compiles the reusable NPM package into \fBdist/\fP with dual format distributions:

.RS 1
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdist/cjs/index\.js\fP (CommonJS format for Node\.js environments and legacy bundlers)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdist/esm/index\.js\fP (ES Module format for modern bundlers and native ESM)

.RE
.P
All JSX is pre\-transpiled to standard \fBReact\.createElement\fP calls, ensuring downstream clients (such as Create React App applications that exclude \fBnode_modules\fP from Babel transpilation) can import the package without encountering raw JSX syntax errors\.
.SS \fBnpm run build:all\fP
.P
Sequentially runs \fBnpm run build:lib\fP and \fBnpm run build\fP to compile both the reusable NPM package and the standalone web application\.
.SS \fBnpm run generate:man\fP (or \fBnpm run man\fP)
.P
Compiles \fBREADME\.md\fP into standard UNIX roff/troff manual documentation format at \fBman/beerbank\.1\fP using \fBmarked\-man\fP\|\.
.SS \fBnpm run eject\fP
.P
\fBNote: this is a one\-way operation\. Once you \fBeject\fP, you can’t go back!\fR
.P
If you aren’t satisfied with the build tool and configuration choices, you can \fBeject\fP at any time\.
.br
This command will remove the single build dependency from your project\.
.P
Instead, it will copy all the configuration files and the transitive dependencies (Webpack, Babel, ESLint, etc) right into your project so you have full control over them\.
.br
All of the commands except \fBeject\fP will still work, but they will point to the copied scripts so you can tweak them\. At this point you’re on your own\.
.P
You don’t have to ever use \fBeject\fP\|\. The curated feature set is suitable for small and middle deployments, and you shouldn’t feel obligated to use this feature\.
.br
However we understand that this tool wouldn’t be useful if you couldn’t customize it when you are ready for it\.
