.SH Integrations
.SS External (NPM Package) Integration
.P
\fB@HolimaX/beerbank\fP is configured as a dual\-distribution NPM package that can be added to any client project's \fBpackage\.json\fP at design time to provide base Cloud Dashboard (CD) functionality for Personalized Cloud Dashboard (PCD) enabled sites (such as \fBHealthDash_GHOrg/CloudDash\-Frontend\-ReactJS\fP)\.
.SS Adding to Client \fBpackage\.json\fP
.P
Add the package under \fBdependencies\fP or \fBoptionalDependencies\fP:
.RS 2
.nf
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@HolimaX/beerbank": "^0\.1\.26"
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.P
Or for local development:
.RS 2
.nf
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@HolimaX/beerbank": "file:\.\./HolimaX_GHOrg/React"
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.SS Client Runtime & Design\-Time Lifecycle Hook
.P
Clients consume the CD foundation module via dynamic \fBimport()\fP or static imports:
.RS 2
.nf
// Dynamic import with design\-time bundling and fallback
const baseModule = await import('@HolimaX/beerbank')\.catch(async () => {
  return await import(/* webpackIgnore: true */ '@HolimaX/beerbank')\.catch(() => null);
});

if (baseModule && typeof baseModule\.myFunction === 'function') {
  const cdStatus = baseModule\.myFunction();
  console\.info("CD Foundation status:", cdStatus);
}
.fi
.RE
.SS Exported Module Inventory
.P
The package exports the following core primitives:

.RS 1
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmyFunction(options)\fP: Base lifecycle initializer returning status, version, and capability flags\.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcomponentIdentityDescriptionAH(version, name)\fP: Component descriptor helper\.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbeerActions\fP: Redux action creators (\fBfetchBeers\fP, \fBfetchBeersWithRetry\fP, \fBsearchBeers\fP, \fBhandleFavourite\fP, \fBfetchPlatformApps\fP, \fBfetchPlatformAppsWithRetry\fP, \fBsearchPlatformapps\fP, \fBdisplayPlatformapp\fP)\.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbeerActionTypes\fP: Complete enumeration of action type constants\.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbeerReducer\fP, \fBrootReducer\fP, \fBstore\fP: Configured Redux state stores and reducers\.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHome\fP, \fBDashboard\fP, \fBFavourites\fP, \fBNavbar\fP, \fBSearch\fP, \fBBeer\fP, \fBBeers\fP, \fBBeerDetails\fP: Pre\-built presentation components\.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBappConfig\fP: Sanitized identity provider and telemetry configuration\.

.RE
.SS CLI & Node REPL Support
.P
To inspect the package interactively in a Node shell or REPL:
.RS 2
.nf
node beerbank
.fi
.RE
.P
Or programmatically in Node\.js / CommonJS scripts:
.RS 2
.nf
const beerbank = require('@HolimaX/beerbank');
console\.log(beerbank\.myFunction());
.fi
.RE
.SS Internal (REST API based) integrations
.P
You can use internal REST API based logic for incoming calls handling for Infrastructure integrated applications\.
.br
The logic consists of Auto\-Synchronization, Auto\-Notification and Auto\-Configuration management for Pro ("Premium") modules\.
.P
Also, the supported method for advanced integration is via C\-style header SO libraries\.
.br
See 
.UR https://medium.com/learning-the-go-programming-language/calling-go-functions-from-other-languages-4c7d8bcc69bf
.I Integration via GoLang
.UE
for details\.
.P
\fBNote: Only CircleCI is building the header files\.\fR
.P
As of now, the infrastructure automation (kubernetes pod) configuration is adjusted in case there is incoming function call from integrated applications\.
.br
This implementation is not aimed to \fB&#39;push&#39;\fP changes, but \fB&#39;pull&#39;\fP instead\.

